<h1 class="docs-title">Blazor.RichTextEditor</h1>
<p class="docs-lede">A flexible WYSIWYG editor for Blazor, powered by Quill.</p>

<div class="docs-meta-row">
    <span class="docs-chip">MIT licensed</span>
    <span class="docs-chip"><code>net10.0</code></span>
    <span class="docs-chip">Server and WebAssembly</span>
</div>

<p>
    <a href="installation">Get started</a> with the installation guide, or
    <a href="components/rich-text-editor">see the examples</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="features">Features</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Reactive editing</strong>: bind HTML, plain text, selection, enabled state, and touched state directly to your Blazor component.</li>
    <li><strong>Flexible toolbars</strong>: start with basic or full presets, move or hide the toolbar, or compose its controls yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Two Quill themes</strong>: choose the conventional Snow toolbar or the selection-driven Bubble interface.</li>
    <li><strong>Large-content mode</strong>: use the passive editor to synchronize large documents and embedded content only when your app needs it.</li>
    <li><strong>Accessible navigation</strong>: opt into keyboard behavior that lets Tab move focus out of the editor instead of indenting content.</li>
</ul>
